<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75980" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρεύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆος</span>, ὁ, 
			Ion.
		 for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρεύς</span> (q. v.): in <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			1.50
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			10.84
		</span></i> it has been taken as, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὖρος, φύλαξ</span>
			, <i>a guard, warder</i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1461a10
			</span></i>; but it may well mean <i>mules</i> here, as in other
			places, and the Sch. give both explanations.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
